665	@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
666	+# 13. An interrupted `version` run resumes from its recorded inputs
667	+
668	+Status: Proposed
669	+
670	+## Context
671	+
672	+- `version` rewrites the files it plans from (manifests, specs, changesets), then refreshes lockfiles. When the refresh fails (E208), a re-run plans from the half-written tree and is refused (E121). The docs name the gap: "a fresh command does not retain that plan" ([versioning](../architecture/versioning.md#idempotent-apply)).
673	+- Release reruns need no recorded state because providers stay observable ([ADR 3](0003-reruns-adopt-landed-effects.md)); a `version` run's inputs are not observable after it has rewritten them.
674	+
675	+## Decision
676	+
677	+Before its first write, `version` records its inputs (`HEAD`, the working tree, the index, and the tags and flags planning reads) as a commit at `refs/callisto/checkpoint/version`, and deletes the ref when the run completes. A re-run while the ref exists plans from those inputs and reapplies idempotently; if an input changed since, it refuses and writes nothing.
678	+
679	+## Options considered
680	+
681	+- **Restore the written files when a step fails** — rejected: each review of #543 found another file state Git already restores correctly (lockfiles from an earlier ecosystem, binary files, symlinks, read-only files).
682	+- **Re-plan from the versions at `HEAD`** — rejected: planning also reads dependency specs from disk, and a prototype resume dropped a dependent the first run had rewritten, exiting 0.
683	+- **Persist the plan itself** — rejected: it must be serialized and versioned and breaks across a Callisto upgrade; recorded inputs can be planned by any version.
684	+
685	+## Consequences
686	+
687	+- A failed refresh, a crash or Ctrl-C is finished by running `version` again.
688	+- One `version` run at a time per repository. CI runners never resume; the ref is lost with the runner.
689	+- The ref name and its recorded fields are read across Callisto versions.
690	+
691	+## Enforcement
692	+
693	+- `crates/callisto-cli/tests/version_resume_tests.rs`: `a_resumed_run_leaves_exactly_what_an_uninterrupted_run_leaves` compares a run whose lockfile refresh fails once and is resumed with one that never failed, across ecosystems, a workspace below the repository root, pre mode and an uncommitted changeset; `changed_inputs_refuse_the_resume_and_the_printed_steps_undo_the_run`; `a_run_that_failed_to_write_its_preview_writes_it_when_run_again`; `a_version_edited_by_hand_after_the_failure_is_refused_not_overwritten`.
694	+- `crates/callisto-model/src/vcs/access.rs`: `a_checkpoint_records_the_tree_leaves_the_user_state_alone_and_is_held_once`.
695	+- VER-APPLY-18 and VER-APPLY-19 in `docs/specs/versioning.json`.
696	+
697	+## Revisit when
698	+
699	+- Planning can read a workspace from git objects without a worktree.
700	+
701	+## Sources
702	+
703	+- PR #543 and its review (change #151, trail #357); E121 and E208 in `docs/errors.md`.
704	+- ADR 3 and PR #124.
705

